# Build output.
/target

# Pre-edit copies. Kept outside the source tree on purpose: a `.bak` beside the
# file it shadows gets read, grepped and occasionally edited by mistake, and
# every one of them is a second copy of code that no longer compiles.
#
# NOT anchored to the root: `docs/.backups/` held 1,291 of them, and a rule that
# only matched `/.backups` let every one into the first commit.
.backups/
*.bak
*.bak.*

# Incord Memory's per-workspace files (RULE_ACK, MEMORY_FIRST_OFF, ...). It is a
# separate product and writes them itself. Unanchored for the same reason as
# `.backups/`: `docs/.incord/` exists too.
.incord/
#
# `.incode/` is NOT ignored here. It holds the owner's approved files
# (contracts.json, guards.json, agents/*.md), which are committed, beside this
# machine's run state (the ledger, transcripts, checkpoints, the server token),
# which is not. incode writes `.incode/.gitignore` to keep the second kind out;
# ignoring the whole folder here would lose the first.
